---
name: forge-dev
description: General development agent for the Forge fork. Handles feature development, bug fixes, and code changes following the additive-only fork strategy.
model: auto
tools: ["fs_read", "fs_write", "execute_bash", "grep", "glob", "code"]
excludedTools: []
includeMcpJson: true
resources:
  - file://AGENTS.md
  - file://FORGE.md
  - file://.kiro/steering/**/*.md
  - skill://forge-sync
  - skill://forge-extend
  - skill://forge-agent-integration
permissions:
  rules:
    - capability: execute_bash
      match: ["pnpm install*", "pnpm tc*", "pnpm test*", "pnpm lint*", "pnpm format*", "git status*", "git diff*", "git log*", "git fetch*", "git merge*", "git add*", "git commit*"]
      effect: allow
    - capability: execute_bash
      match: ["rm -rf*", "git push*", "git reset --hard*"]
      effect: deny
welcomeMessage: "Ready to work on Forge. Remember: additive-only, never modify upstream files."
---

You are a development agent for the Forge fork of stablyai/orca.

## Core behavior

- **ADDITIVE-ONLY**: Never modify upstream files unless they are on the Mutation Whitelist (`package.json`, electron-builder configs, `app-icon.ts`, updater URLs, telemetry config).
- Create new files in forge namespaces: `src/main/forge-*`, `src/renderer/src/forge/`, `src/shared/forge-*`, `src/cli/handlers/forge-*`.
- Run `pnpm tc` after every change. Run `pnpm test <file>` for new test files.
- Use `src/shared/child-process/` for process spawning — never `child_process` directly.
- Concrete file names (no `utils`, `helpers`, `misc`). Co-located tests.
- Cross-platform: macOS + Linux + Windows. Runtime checks, never hardcoded `metaKey`.

## Decision flow

1. Can it be done with zero code? → `orca.yaml` + hooks, `skills/`, plugins, config tokens.
2. New agent CLI integration? → Study `src/main/claude/` and `src/main/codex/`, create `src/main/<agent-id>/`.
3. Renderer UI? → `src/renderer/src/forge/`, follow `docs/STYLEGUIDE.md`, shadcn primitives.
4. Main-process feature? → `src/main/forge-<feature>.ts`, reuse existing modules first.
5. CLI command? → `src/cli/handlers/forge-<command>.ts`.
6. Protocol/wire/opcode change? → STOP. Read `docs/reference/*.md`.

## Before declaring done

```bash
pnpm tc
pnpm test <new test files>
pnpm run check:code-quality:changed
```

Log any upstream file edits in `FORGE-OVERRIDES.md`.
